## Validation and decision

[Repair verification](repair-verification.json) records the final hashes and
commands. The checks comprise 12 retained arithmetic illustrations, 49 exact
repair/conformance checks and 31 core-contract/reference checks. These 92
assertions have different, overlapping scopes; their total is inventory, not
an acceptance score. The PDF has 79 pages and the library has 32 paper PDFs.
All rendered pages were inspected through contact sheets, with detailed
inspection of the case tables, solver passage, code, sector equations,
appendix records and bibliography. Confirmed pagination and spacing defects
were repaired. No old display equation or citation key was removed.

| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto status | Main uncertainty | Next justified action | What does not follow |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Deliver the revised design candidate | Each G finding has a concrete repair, evidence and residual obligation; MC wording retained | No known failed local arithmetic/build check; source gaps qualify the affected treatments | Independent implementability, accounting and human comprehension remain untested | Build the bounded shared-IR compiler/validator and reference path; obtain the missing domain evidence alongside extension work | Whole mission complete, compliant accounting engine, representative real-company reconstruction, or forecast superiority |

The strongest alternative explanation for apparent progress is that authored
fixtures and author review share the same assumptions as the manuscript. Exact
solver counterexamples, preserved source bytes and independent recomputation
reduce some errors but cannot remove that risk. Independent implementation and
accounting review could expose missing semantics or wrong treatment; those
findings must reopen the relevant requirements. Page count, successful
compilation and more citations cannot overturn such findings.

The plan was completed as a local repair campaign with the stated residuals;
the broader audit is **not** declared fully closed. Missing human/domain
feedback blocks final acceptance, not further provisional work. No production
engine, benchmark, stochastic comparison, deployment or external communication
was undertaken.
